# QA M6 BUG (fails on purpose until fixed): holding LEFT after the Bad Ischl
# checkpoint respawn walks Resi into the Traun and dies, again and again
# (the M4 "holding LEFT after a checkpoint respawn" class; Strobl was
# designed against it, D-097 addendum item 4). bad_ischl_checkpoint's
# inputs to its death in file B (1266) and the respawn at the Esplanade
# checkpoint (col 152, x 2434, 1326, camera x 2296). Then LEFT is held: she
# walks left along the landing 147-151 and drops into landing notch 2
# (cols 143-146, lethal salzach_water) at 1403, 77 frames after the
# respawn, before the screen's left edge (2296) can stop her: the notch is
# 5 columns left of the respawn point and inside the respawn screen. The
# same at the next respawn (1540), then game over (RUN held too: 56 frames).
# Expected: a respawned Resi who holds LEFT is stopped on solid ground
# (the landing, x >= 2352) and does not die; e.g. a checkpoint further
# right, or a respawn camera whose left edge is right of the notch.
level  = bad_ischl
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=1 dies_at frames=1266..1266 lives=2 state=playing player_x>=2352 no_event=GameOver
